      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:2:48:7",
      "text": [
        " سَمِعْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) يَقُولُ لَوْ أَنَّ رَجُلًا مَاتَ صَائِماً فِي السَّفَرِ مَا صَلَّيْتُ عَلَيْهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Salma Bin Al Khattab, from Suleyman Bin Sama’at, from Ali Bin Ismail, from Muhammad Bin Hakeym who said, ",
          "‘I heard Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> saying: ‘If a man were to die whilst Fasting during the journey, I<sup>asws</sup> would not Pray over him’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "7. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Salmah ibn al-Khattab from Sulayman ibn Sama‘ah, from Ali ibn ‘Isma‘il from Muhammad ibn Hakim who has said the following: “I once heard abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, say, ‘If a man while on a journey and fasting dies, I will not perform Salat (prayer) (of dead people) for him.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
